+# TASK-260720-1qhxqa developer handoff — revision 5
+
+Status: ready for independent review.
+
+## Blocking review finding resolved
+
+CR revision 4 correctly showed that changed upstream bytes plus a synchronized
+manifest digest could retain production permission. The immutable normalized
+trust root now includes all eight accepted M0/M1 outcome and reviewer-verdict
+SHA-256 values. Board-owned bytes are still recomputed separately, so neither
+the resource nor the mutable manifest can self-authorize a replacement.
+
+The production entry point is `make m0-bindings-check`, which invokes
+`scripts/validate-m0-production-bindings.py`. The new synchronized-digest
+narrowing test changes the accepted packet/HEV outcome bytes, updates the
+manifest digest to match, drives that exact CLI, and requires exit 1,
+`productionCompositionPermitted=false`, and stable row `NORMALIZED-CONTRACT`.
+
+## Exact accepted bindings
+
+- Machine manifest: `Configuration/TASK-260720-1qhxqa_m0-production-bindings-v1.json`.
+- Manifest SHA-256: `39b3428d6cf778fa6b682bb0853a177d6b85f03b8062309f0d198dcdfd49fae6`.
+- Immutable normalized contract SHA-256:
+  `3bedf4fc9b6747512a89e9910d686b98f915e4240dfb050f2a4b2915a4e9cf44`.
+- Every one of the eight exact accepted outcome/verdict resource digests was
+  independently recomputed and matched.
+- Repository, owning task attachment, and `TASK-260715-3ejhyy` sole-consumer
+  precondition are byte-identical.
+- Every authority remains `done`; all supersession states remain `current`;
+  all exact normalized graph, packet/HEV, SSH, license/maintenance,
+  revalidation, compatibility, and consumer rows remain unchanged.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Targeted synchronized-digest production-entry regression: exit 0 (test
+  passed; the nested validator refusal is asserted).
+- Full binding suite: exit 0, 17/17 tests passed.
+- Authoritative baseline `make m0-bindings-check`: exit 0, no failures,
+  `productionCompositionPermitted=true`.
+- Python compile, tracked diff check, and untracked whitespace check: exit 0.
+- Independent eight-resource SHA-256 comparison: exit 0.
+- Owner/repository/consumer byte identity: exit 0.
+- `task-board validate`: process exit 0 and three retained
+  `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` rows. Owning Story `STORY-260715-1y04r0` is stored
+  `to-dev` while its child aggregate is `development`; two unrelated Stories
+  are also mismatched. Raw evidence is attached and is not represented as a
+  clean board validation.
+
+No M0 implementation was copied, no implementation or tuning selection was
+performed, and `TASK-260715-3ejhyy` remains the sole consumer of this manifest.
